---
// Tax Liens Hero
---

<section id="hero" class="relative bg-dark-background py-20 lg:py-28 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute inset-0">
    <img src="/assets/images/pexels/pexels-photo-30255750-1200.jpeg"
      srcset="/assets/images/pexels/pexels-photo-30255750-320.jpeg 320w, /assets/images/pexels/pexels-photo-30255750-640.jpeg 640w, /assets/images/pexels/pexels-photo-30255750-1024.jpeg 1024w, /assets/images/pexels/pexels-photo-30255750-1920.jpeg 1920w"
      sizes="100vw"
      alt="Federal and State Tax Liens Defense"
      class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-35"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-black/85 via-black/70 to-black/85"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="relative max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 text-center">
    <div class="inline-block bg-[#C1272D] text-white font-medium text-[12px] uppercase tracking-wider px-3 py-1 rounded-[6px] mb-4">
      Tax Lien Release & Subordination
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-[40px] lg:text-[56px] font-bold text-white font-serif mb-4 leading-[1.1] max-w-[950px] mx-auto">
      Federal and State Tax Liens
    </h1>
    <p class="text-[18px] lg:text-[22px] text-gray-200 italic max-w-[850px] mx-auto leading-relaxed">
      When you owe taxes, a tax lien may be filed against your Utah property. Call our Utah Tax Lien Attorneys today.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
